  "title": "Tomato Rounds With Garlic & Cheese",
  "description": "Please don't use store-bought shredded cheese, it will not taste the same trust me, it is not so hard to shred the cheese after all.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It's a super simple and fantastic 10 minutes appetizers, that I could eat a plateful. And when it comes to cheese, you are the boss. You can choose any hard/firm cheese that you like, as long as you'll be able to grate it. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21599,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1659207727979} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21599-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Tomato Rounds With Garlic &amp; Cheese</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/IMG_9146.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tPlease don't use  store-bought shredded cheese, it will not taste the same trust me, it is not so hard to shred the cheese after all.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>4-6 tomatoes</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper (to aste)</li><li>1 clove garlic</li><li>100 g hard cheese</li><li>some olive oil ((optional))</li><li>some  fresh herbs (parsley, green onion, dill, )</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Wash and cut the tomatoes into circles and layer them on the plater. Sprinkle with some salt and pepper to taste.</li><li>Grate garlic, using microplane, sprinkle it on top of the tomatoes. Using the same microplane shred the cheese. Evenly layer on top of the tomatoes.</li><li>Drizzle with some olive oil and garnish with fresh herbs.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/04/IMG_9147.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Appetizers</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
